unity david du is  the co-founder of arena technology his  team with the help from singapore's  national environment agency has created  a system to help scientists breed male  mosquitoes they are injected with a  bacteria called walbukia and then  released into an environment to mate  with female mosquitoes causing them to  lay eggs that do not hatch many  companies want to use this technique but  counting as well as sorting the males  and females can be extremely laborious  the larvae dispensing system quickly  counts the larvae and the pupae  separation system sorts the sexes we  hope more industries could adopt our  technology to improve public health and  quality of life  helping people live a better life is at  the core of this next singapore-based  invention  it's all about giving an extra hand  due to aging population we have more and  more people with stroke causing physical  damage by using soft robotic  technologies we can make something new  that's very portable and easy to use my  name is jin wang i'm the co-founder and  ceo of processor technologies this is  called iso glove which is a soft robotic  hand glove for people with neurological  disorders and eventually may have hand  impairments we have selected one  specific material a very light fabric we  also have a control box to provide the  power and the air into the glove and  together with our software we are able  to provide hand rehabilitation therapy  so far we have been trying our device on  hundreds of patients in different  continents so we have seen very positive  outcomes from very mild patients all the  way to serious stroke patients there are  a lot of problems in the world  especially health care problems so if we  can utilize innovations to help people  recover much faster we can improve the  quality of life of all the people who  are affected with diseases or  disabilities  now onto a light bulb moment that's  bringing power to rural regions  more than 2 billion people  have very limited access to electricity  a lot of these people use kerosene lamps  there are many accidents that happen and  it's not very environmentally friendly  our solar lantern solves all these  problems my name is hari haram and i'm  the founder and ceo of third wave power  this is the solar lantern the solar  panel is the primary element that  actually collects energy it's exposed to  the sun and energy goes into the battery  the battery stores the energy during the  day when the lantern switches on the led  will start consuming the energy from the  battery we also use a battery technology  called the lfp batteries that lasts for  nearly four to five years so it's  definitely way more efficient way more  safe the impact that solar powered  applications can create in the future is  far greater than what we have achieved  today and it's only the beginning of the  journey  and finally a device that uses a  different kind of light to empower those  without access to what many people take  for granted there's a lot of areas in  the world that don't have good access to  internet simply because building  infrastructure in those places is too  expensive we believe everyone regardless  of where they're living should have  access to the internet that's why we're  building the centauri technology the  centauri one is a laser communication  device that can help people get access  to super fast internet it uses state of  the art laser communication technology  all you need to do is go on a rooftop  mount the device point it towards the  closest location nearby where you do  have access to internet you put another  one of these devices on that rooftop as  well the lasers will find themselves and  boom you have a fiber like connection  between the two buildings  our ultimate goal is to build a global  network of satellites using lasers to  connect every single place on the planet  to each other so that's the way we see  ourself growing in the future  connectivity for everyone  [Music]
 

